& [FixturePlan: FSC4SurfaceProjectionFixturePlanV1] is the bounded fixture plan for FSC4 surface projection
  + [slice_id] is FSC4-S06
  + [fixture_family] is surface-projection-authority-notice
  + [fixture_case_count] is 11
  + [fixture_index] is docs/fixtures/FSC4_Surface_Projection_Fixture_Index.v1.sop
  + [model_route] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable

  = must: treat this plan as fixture planning, not executable test harness implementation
  = must: cover manager, worker, narrative, debug, conversation, adapter, Langflow, divergence, and completion gate projection paths
  - never: implement UI, adapters, transports, Langflow export, runtime services, dispatch, or operations control here

& [FixtureCase: F4X-001-manager-ready-packet] is the manager ready packet projection fixture
  + [input_shape] is ready work state with accepted packet, fresh boundary input, no contested claim, and accepted completion review gate
  + [expected_projection] is manager_summary_projection with authority_notice_ref, freshness_state fresh, current_ready_slice_or_chunk, source_lineage_ref_set, and available_action_route_set
  + [expected_visibility] is readiness, support_delta, requirement_delta, claim state, and completion_review_ref visible
  + [expected_refusal_absent] is assignment, dispatch, direct gate mutation, and completion acceptance
  + [acceptance_status] is accepted

& [FixtureCase: F4X-002-worker-blocked-packet] is the worker blocked packet projection fixture
  + [input_shape] is work_packet_ref with unresolved support_gap or forbidden_scope mismatch
  + [expected_projection] is worker_packet_projection with blocked_projection status, authority_notice_ref, blocker_ref_set, required_resolution, and forbidden_scope_set
  + [expected_visibility] is no completion claim action and no false ready display
  + [expected_route] is support repair, scope rebake, SOP-first interrupt, or completion review gate
  + [acceptance_status] is blocked

& [FixtureCase: F4X-003-stale-projection] is the stale projection fixture
  + [input_shape] is projection whose accepted boundary pack hash or source freshness fails
  + [expected_projection] is stale_projection with freshness_state stale, stale_source_ref_set, invalidation_ref_set, and authority_notice_ref
  + [expected_visibility] is stale state appears before any authority-sensitive action
  + [expected_route] is refresh accepted input or rerun completion review
  + [acceptance_status] is stale

& [FixtureCase: F4X-004-narrative-lineage] is the narrative lineage projection fixture
  + [input_shape] is narrative projection from project narrative, conversation surface, completion review, support delta, and reentry packet records
  + [expected_projection] is narrative_projection with source_lineage_ref_set, open_frontier_set, blocked_or_stale_context_set, and reentry_packet_ref_set
  + [expected_visibility] is stale or incomplete narrative context remains visible
  + [expected_refusal_absent] is source narrative rewrite, canonical rewrite, completion acceptance, and gate mutation
  + [acceptance_status] is accepted

& [FixtureCase: F4X-005-debug-fault-trace] is the debug fault trace projection fixture
  + [input_shape] is operator_trace_ref_set with fault_record_ref, missing trace field, or hidden_write_prevention evidence
  + [expected_projection] is debug_trace_projection with trace_path_summary, fault_summary_set, unresolved_debug_question_set, and authority_notice_ref
  + [expected_visibility] is missing trace fields become projection_fault or blocked debug projection
  + [expected_refusal_absent] is fault repair, trace mutation, checkpoint authority promotion, and runtime execution
  + [acceptance_status] is blocked

& [FixtureCase: F4X-006-conversation-interrupt] is the conversation interrupt projection fixture
  + [input_shape] is conversation projection carrying ambiguous or authority-sensitive inbound action from a participant
  + [expected_projection] is conversation_projection with interrupt_context_ref, visible_authority_notice, visible_freshness_state, carrier_surface, and conversation_lineage_ref_set
  + [expected_route] is SOP-first interrupt with carrier context preserved
  + [expected_refusal_absent] is participant identity collapse, direct authority mutation, and completion review acceptance
  + [acceptance_status] is interrupted

& [FixtureCase: F4X-007-adapter-mutation-refusal] is the adapter mutation refusal fixture
  + [input_shape] is adapter-originated work_request, claim_request, review_request, interrupt_resolution_request, or human_override_request attempting direct source mutation
  + [expected_projection] is adapter_event_projection with inbound_action_classification, mutation_gate_ref, authority_notice_ref, and blocked_route evidence
  + [expected_route] is action_request, coordination_request, interrupt_context, or completion_review_request
  + [expected_refusal] is direct canonical write, accepted pack write, completion review acceptance, job dispatch, and operations command
  + [acceptance_status] is blocked

& [FixtureCase: F4X-008-missing-authority-notice] is the missing authority notice fixture
  + [input_shape] is decision-making projection without authority_notice_ref
  + [expected_projection] is projection_fault_record or blocked_projection
  + [expected_visibility] is missing_authority_notice appears as refusal reason
  + [expected_route] is repair projection contract output before use
  + [acceptance_status] is faulted

& [FixtureCase: F4X-009-langflow-non-authority-projection] is the Langflow non-authority projection fixture
  + [input_shape] is Langflow graph projection displaying executable-looking graph or operator flow
  + [expected_projection] is langflow_graph_projection with authority_notice_ref, authority_limit explanatory only, freshness_state, and lineage_edge_set
  + [expected_visibility] is graph projection cannot be mistaken for executable authority
  + [expected_refusal_absent] is Langflow installation, Langflow export implementation, runtime execution, or source authority mutation
  + [acceptance_status] is accepted

& [FixtureCase: F4X-010-multi-surface-divergence] is the multi-surface divergence fixture
  + [input_shape] is two or more carrier projections with authority_notice mismatch, hidden fault state, stale projection, inconsistent claim state, carrier ordering conflict, or missing lineage
  + [expected_projection] is divergence_notice plus stale_projection, coordination_conflict_signal, or sop_first_interrupt_context
  + [expected_visibility] is per-surface evidence set remains available
  + [expected_route] is reconcile source freshness, claim state, lineage, or interrupt before authority-sensitive action
  + [acceptance_status] is stale

& [FixtureCase: F4X-011-completion-gate-refusal] is the completion gate refusal fixture
  + [input_shape] is projected follow-on action attempting to open FSC5 without accepted FSC4 completion review and surface projection pack
  + [expected_projection] is blocked_projection with completion_review_ref missing, required_resolution, authority_notice_ref, and downstream_gate closed
  + [expected_visibility] is FSC5 remains gated
  + [expected_route] is FSC4-S07 completion review and activation packet
  + [acceptance_status] is blocked

